WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.513
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.813 --> 00:00:09.118
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.418 --> 00:00:15.832
Unit twenty-one: Likes and Dislikes (like + -ing). Today you will talk about what you like and dislike doing.

4
00:00:16.132 --> 00:00:18.610
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:22.602
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.358
Like.

7
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.164
Like means to enjoy something.

8
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:28.902
I like music.

9
00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:31.554
Your turn. Say: Like.

10
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.146
Like.

11
00:00:35.883 --> 00:00:36.710
Love.

12
00:00:37.717 --> 00:00:40.123
Love means to like something very much.

13
00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:42.020
I love dancing.

14
00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:45.014
Your turn. Say: Love.

15
00:00:47.867 --> 00:00:48.636
Love.

16
00:00:49.383 --> 00:00:50.059
Hate.

17
00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.514
Hate means to dislike something very much.

18
00:00:54.117 --> 00:00:55.327
I hate waiting.

19
00:00:55.917 --> 00:00:57.954
Your turn. Say: Hate.

20
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:01.604
Hate.

21
00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:03.374
Don't like.

22
00:01:04.383 --> 00:01:06.580
Don't like means not to enjoy something.

23
00:01:07.183 --> 00:01:08.765
I don't like spiders.

24
00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.805
Your turn. Say: Don't like.

25
00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:15.703
Don't like.

26
00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:17.370
Swimming.

27
00:01:18.383 --> 00:01:20.812
Swimming means moving through water for fun.

28
00:01:21.417 --> 00:01:22.638
Swimming is fun.

29
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.647
Your turn. Say: Swimming.

30
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:29.397
Swimming.

31
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:30.965
Reading.

32
00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:34.588
Reading means looking at words and understanding them.

33
00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:36.707
Reading is relaxing.

34
00:01:37.317 --> 00:01:39.772
Your turn. Say: Reading.

35
00:01:42.633 --> 00:01:43.449
Reading.

36
00:01:44.183 --> 00:01:44.999
Dancing.

37
00:01:45.983 --> 00:01:47.936
Dancing means moving to music.

38
00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:50.120
Dancing makes me happy.

39
00:01:50.717 --> 00:01:52.939
Your turn. Say: Dancing.

40
00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:56.615
Dancing.

41
00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.154
Playing.

42
00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:01.289
Playing means doing something for fun.

43
00:02:01.883 --> 00:02:03.511
Playing football is fun.

44
00:02:04.117 --> 00:02:06.444
Your turn. Say: Playing.

45
00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.034
Playing.

46
00:02:10.833 --> 00:02:14.716
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:18.316
Visal, what do you like doing at the weekend?

48
00:02:19.417 --> 00:02:31.002
I like swimming and reading. After like, love and hate, we can use a verb with -ing: I like swimming. She loves dancing. He hates waiting.

49
00:02:32.117 --> 00:02:34.302
How do we say we do not enjoy something?

50
00:02:35.417 --> 00:02:45.572
We say don't like or doesn't like: I don't like cooking. She doesn't like running. We can also say hate for a very strong feeling.

51
00:02:46.683 --> 00:02:48.381
Is there a quick scale?

52
00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:58.721
Yes: love, like, don't like, hate. From very positive to very negative. After each one use the -ing form to talk about activities.

53
00:02:59.867 --> 00:03:01.448
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:02.283 --> 00:03:06.222
Grammar focus: Like and love and hate plus verb-ing.

55
00:03:06.522 --> 00:03:07.697
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:08.383 --> 00:03:09.675
I like swimming.

57
00:03:10.583 --> 00:03:11.979
She loves dancing.

58
00:03:12.883 --> 00:03:14.326
He doesn't like cooking.

59
00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:23.271
After like, love, hate and don't like, use the -ing form of the verb to talk about activities. Add s to like and love with he, she and it.

60
00:03:24.017 --> 00:03:27.087
Be careful! Don't say: I like swim.

61
00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.673
Say: I like swimming.

62
00:03:30.973 --> 00:03:33.007
Use verb + -ing after like.

63
00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:36.696
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.826
What I Like Doing.

65
00:03:39.126 --> 00:03:41.520
I love dancing and I like playing football.

66
00:03:42.533 --> 00:03:45.671
My sister likes reading, but she doesn't like cooking.

67
00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.759
My brother hates waking up early.

68
00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:51.697
We both like swimming in the river.

69
00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.013
Everyone has different likes and dislikes.

70
00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.647
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:01.483 --> 00:04:03.123
She loves blank music.

72
00:04:03.423 --> 00:04:07.297
A, listen to. B, listening to. C, listens to.

73
00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:13.007
The answer is B: listening to.

74
00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:15.801
I don't like blank early.

75
00:04:16.101 --> 00:04:19.685
A, get up. B, getting up. C, gets up.

76
00:04:23.233 --> 00:04:24.908
The answer is B: getting up.

77
00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.783
He blank playing games.

78
00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:31.248
A, like. B, likes. C, liking.

79
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.579
The answer is B: likes.

80
00:04:37.717 --> 00:04:39.240
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:44.018
A, I like swim.. B, I like swimming.. C, I like to swimming..

82
00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:49.984
The answer is B: I like swimming..

83
00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:54.229
According to the reading, who hates waking up early?

84
00:04:54.529 --> 00:04:58.125
A, my brother. B, my sister. C, the writer.

85
00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.446
The answer is A: my brother.

86
00:05:04.633 --> 00:05:07.750
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:08.617 --> 00:05:10.465
What do you like doing at the weekend?

88
00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.774
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:21.074 --> 00:05:35.388
At the weekend I like reading books and playing football with my friends. I also love swimming when the weather is hot. I don't like cleaning, but I do it. After like I use the -ing form of the verb.

90
00:05:35.688 --> 00:05:37.258
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:43.124
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and like and love and hate plus verb-ing.

92
00:05:43.424 --> 00:05:47.180
Today's value is passion. Find what you love and practise it.

93
00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:50.190
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:53.073
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

